    "content": "Max Strus (born March 28, 1996) is a 29-year-old NBA shooting guard/small forward for the Cleveland Cavaliers, known for his elite 3-point shooting and high-energy play. After missing most of the 2025-26 season with a foot injury, he returned in March 2026 to average 8.8 points and shoot over 40% from deep. Key Details Current Team: Cleveland Cavaliers (#2). Position: Shooting Guard / Small Forward. Age: 29 (born March 28, 1996). NBA Teams: Chicago Bulls (2019-20), Miami Heat (2020-23), Cleveland Cavaliers (2023-present). Career Highlights: 2023 NBA Finalist (Heat), signed 4-year, $62.3M contract with Cavs in 2023, 59-foot buzzer-beater vs. Mavericks. College: Lewis University (DII) and DePaul University (DI). Draft: Undrafted in 2019. 2025-2026 Season & Return Strus underwent surgery for a Jones fracture in his left foot, missing the first 67 games of the 2025-26 season. He made an explosive return on March 15, 2026, scoring 24 points (6-of-7 3PT) in 22 minutes against the Dallas Mavericks. Since his return, he has averaged 8.8 points and 40.9% 3PT shooting, adding significant floor spacing for the Cavaliers' postseason push. This video discusses Max Strus's return to the court after his injury:06:08It's Cavalier PodcastYouTube• Mar 6, 2026 06:08 Previous Seasons 2023-24 (Cavs): In his first season with Cleveland, he played 70 games, averaging 12.2 points, 4.8 rebounds, and 4.0 assists while starting every game he played. 2022-23 (Heat): A key role player in Miami's run to the NBA Finals.",
